   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the New York state urban development corporation act, in\nrelation to the regional revolving loan program",
    "basePrintNo": "S7299",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7299-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 7,
       "fullName": "Elaine Phillips",
       "imgName": "no_image.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1100,
       "sessionMemberId": 1096,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "PHILLIPS"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§16-a, 16-c, 16-d & 16-t, UDC Act (as proposed in S. 4046 and A. 4253)",
    "lawSection": "New York State Urban Development Corporation Act",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7299\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the New York state urban development\ncorporation act, in relation to the regional revolving loan program\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would adjust from January 2018 to April 1, 2019 the date upon\nwhich the New York State Empire State Development Corporation (ESDC)\nshall publish annual reports relating to the Regional Revolving Loan\nTrust Fund Program, Minority and Women Revolving Loan Trust Fund\nProgram, Micro Enterprise Revolving Loan Trust Fund and Commercial\nDistrict Revolving Loan Trust fund program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend subdivision 20 of section 16-a of section 1 of\nchapter 174 of the laws of 1968, constituting the New York state urban\ndevelopment corporation act as amended by a chapter of the laws of 2017,\namending the New York state urban development corporation act relating\nto the regional revolving loan program; amend subparagraphs (i) and (ii)\nof paragraph (i) of subdivision 2 of 11 section 16-c of section 1 of\nchapter 174 of the laws of 1968, constituting the New York state urban\ndevelopment corporation act, as added by a chapter of the laws of 2017,\namending the New York state urban development corporation act relating\nto the regional revolving loan program; amend paragraph (e) of subdivi-\nsion 3 of section 16-c of section 1 of 2 chapter 174 of the laws of\n1968, constituting the New York state urban development corporation act,\nas added by a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the New York state\nurban development corporation act relating to the regional revolving\nloan program; amend paragraph (c) of subdivision 14 of section 16-d of\nsection 1 of 20 chapter 174 of the laws of 1968, constituting the New\nYork state urban development corporation act, as added by a chapter of\nthe laws of 2017, amending the New York state urban development corpo-\nration act relating to the regional revolving loan program; amend para-\ngraph (c) of subdivision 14 of section 16-d of section 1 of chapter 174\nof the laws of 1968, constituting the New York state urban development\ncorporation act, as added by a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the\nNew York state urban development corporation act relating to the\nregional revolving loan program; amend subdivisions 14 and 14-a of\nsection 16-t of section 1 of chapter 174 of the laws of 1968, constitut-\ning the New York state urban development corporation act, subdivision 14\nas amended and subdivision 14-a as added by a chapter of the laws of\n2017, amending the New York state urban development corporation act\nrelating to the regional revolving loan program to adjust from January\n2018 to April 1, 2019 the date upon which New York State Empire State\nDevelopment Corporation (ESDC)shall publish its annual reports relating\nto the Regional Revolving Loan Trust Fund Program, Minority and Women\nRevolving Loan Trust Fund Program, Micro Enterprise Revolving Loan Trust\nFund and Commercial District Revolving Loan Trust fund program.\n\nThis bill would also amend the effective date to take effect on the same\ndate and in the same manner as a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending\nthe New York state urban development corporation act relating to the\nregional revolving loan program, as proposed in legislative bill numbers\nS4046 and A4253, takes effect.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2017: A. 4253/S. 4046\n2015-16: A.7517-A/S.5494-A\n2014: A.10065\n\n \nSTATEMENT IN SUPPORT:\n\nThis bill would allow the ESDC to administer the Regional Revolving Loan\nTrust Fund Program, Minority and Women Revolving Loan Trust Fund\nProgram, Micro Enterprise Revolving Loan Trust Fund and Commercial\nDistrict Revolving Loan Trust fund in a manner consistent with the small\nbusiness revolving loan fund program. This will allow ESDC greater flex-\nibility to structure transactions that more closely meet changing market\nrequirements, while still servicing the types of businesses that all of\nthe Revolving Loan Fund Programs are intended to benefit.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2017, amending the New York state urban develop-\nment corporation act relating to the regional revolving loan program, as\nproposed in legislative bill numbers S4046 and A4253, takes effect.\n",
